			       STANDARD MOUSE MENU


The MSMENU Mouse Menu lets you use the mouse with applications (including
DOS) that don't normally support the mouse. To use this menu, you need to
load it into memory before you start your application.  See the general
instructions above for loading a mouse menu.

MSMENU Button Functions

Once MSMENU is loaded, the mouse moves the cursor like the cursor keys do.
The buttons on the mouse work as follows:


	 Left Button Click  - Your choice:  the first time you press the left
			      button, a menu will come up and you can choose
			      to assign a key to the left button (i.e., Q&A
			      uses the F10 key in all it's menus to continue
			      the operation).  If you want to assign a
			      combination of keys (SHIFT, CTRL or ALT +)
			      highlight and click right on one of these
			      choices and an additional menu will come up to
			      complete the request.  Now the left button will
			      be the key you selected until you re-assign the
			      the button or unload MSMENU.

	 Right Button Click - Same as <Enter>

	 Both Buttons Click - Same as <Esc>

	 Right Double Click - Displays the left button definition menu.  You
			      can re-assign the left button to a new key while
			      you are still in your program.


  You can adjust the sensitivity of the mouse movement by using the CPANEL
  program.  See the "Microsoft Mouse User's Guide" for instructions.





























